diff --git a/features/conformance/dom-identity.feature b/features/conformance/dom-identity.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8baeae8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/conformance/dom-identity.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+Feature: DOM identity preservation
+
+  When the todo list state changes (toggle, add, remove, edit) the render
+  function MUST mutate existing DOM nodes in place — toggle classes, set
+  .checked, update textContent — rather than rebuilding the list from
+  scratch via innerHTML. Rebuilding destroys every existing <li> node,
+  which detaches any browser-held reference and causes Cypress
+  acceptance tests to fail with "element detached from DOM".
+
+  The fix: replace `todoList.innerHTML = html` with a diff loop that
+  reuses existing <li> elements.
+
+  @captain @conformance
+  Scenario: Render function does not rebuild the todo list via innerHTML
+    Given the project has a render function that writes to the todo list
+    When I check whether the render function assigns innerHTML on the todo-list container
+    Then the render function does not use innerHTML reassignment on the todo list
+
+  @captain @conformance
+  Scenario: Render function mutates existing nodes in place for completion toggles
+    Given the project has a render function that handles completion state
+    When I check whether a completion toggle triggers a full innerHTML rebuild
+    Then a completion toggle does not rebuild the list via innerHTML
